WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.840
I had a limited amount of suffering.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.560
OK, I was tortured and so on,

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.600
many people suffered
far worse than me.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.840
The Archbishop of Canterbury's
special envoy, Terry Waite,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.400
hasn't been seen
for more than 24 hours.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.240
Fears are growing that he may be held
against his will in West Beirut.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.560
Where he's been trying to negotiate
the release of more hostages.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.200
I had nothing.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.560
I never saw the sun, or the sky
or felt the wind on my face.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.560
That's an extreme situation.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.720
But from extreme situations

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.280
you can take something
that is applicable to normal life.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:52.520
Initially I was kept underground, in
the cell, and then later on,
bombed-out buildings.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.640
I slept on the floor.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.520
And had nothing.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.480
And I just had to say,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.640
"How am I going
to utilise this time?"

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.160
"What am I going to do?"

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.360
I wrote a short poem about anger.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.960
Because I was angry at times, and
I had to learn how to master anger.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.200
And the short poem reads...

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.320
What I was really saying is that

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.400
if I allow my understandable anger
to get the better of me,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:38.720
it'll destroy me.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.200
And it's a natural human force,
we all have it.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.960
You can't obliterate it totally.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.480
But take that force
and utilise it constructively.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.000
I used to say to myself,

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.960
although you're in restricted
and limiting circumstances,

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.520
and you've no idea whether
you're going to be out tomorrow,

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.800
whether you're going
to be out in five years,

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.640
whether you're going to die in
this place, remember one thing...

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.320
Not tomorrow, not yesterday, now.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.480
And in this moment,
don't be defeated.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.440
There's no reason
to feel sorry for yourself.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.520
After 1,763 days in chains,

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.560
it's an overwhelming experience

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:40.440
to come back
and receive your greetings.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.320
I thought those years in captivity

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.240
were totally wasted.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.320
At the time.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.000
But looking back, they weren't.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Because I was forced there
to use my imagination.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.960
I was forced... I wrote
my first book in my head.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.000
The brain is like a muscle.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.920
You use it, or you lose it.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.800
Today, it's a great regret to me

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.360
that the arts, music,
literature, poetry,

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.840
are seen as not being
really necessary.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.960
Because at times of life,

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.240
you need to have in your mind
something that you can draw on.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.400
Something that you can refer to.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.920
Something that will
fill out your life.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.760
So many people are suffering
from mental illness.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.120
From strain, from stress,

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.840
from having so much

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.880
pressure forced on them.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.840
And somehow we need,
today more than ever,

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.160
this ability to be at peace
with ourselves within.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:02.440
I'm not sure whether ever one reaches
a state of complete happiness.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.640
It's an elusive term really.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.920
I suppose all I can strive for

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.560
is to have a greater degree
of inner contentment.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.360
Which is in fact part
of the road towards happiness.

